<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Kingdom of Portugal, Brazil and the Algarves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815–1825</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarves</a> was the monarchy created in December 1815, when the Portuguese court, which had fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> in 1807, raised Brazil from a colony to a kingdom equal with Portugal. Maria I and then John VI ruled it from Rio until 1821. Brazil declared independence under his son Pedro in 1822, and Portugal recognised it in 1825, ending the union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-kingdom-of-portugal-brazil-and-the-algarves.jpg" alt="United Kingdom of Portugal, Brazil and the Algarves" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 117-M-I-K-E · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_of_Portugal,_Brazil,_and_the_Algarves_(1815-1825).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
